    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey so im working with a client who's pretty much stuck on their squat. been at the same weight for like 3 weeks now and they cant seem to move past it. can u explain how doing a deload week or messing with the volume might actually help them break through that plateau?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "A deload week can be beneficial in helping your client break through their squat plateau. By reducing the overall volume and intensity of their training for 1-2 weeks, they can allow their body to focus on recovery and rebuild before attempting the squat again. This can also help eliminate any athletes blockages, allowing their nervous system to mobilize and generate more power. Additionally, incorporating a lower-volume curtsy squat or front squat session during their deload week may also help.",
      "source": "target",
