    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "got it. so it's basically just neurological fatigue and efficiency. is there anything else that causes these types of plateaus? like are there any other specific variables besides CNS fatigue or volume that we should be looking at to figure out why they aren't progressing?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Besides CNS fatigue and volume, other variables that can contribute to plateaus include technique-based inefficiencies, muscle imbalances, and joint issues. Poor squat mechanics, such as had hip extension or failed lockout, can limit force production and prevent progress. Muscle imbalances, like weak quads or tight hamstrings, can alter movement patterns and reduce power output. Additionally, joint issues, like chronic stiffness or joint pain, can impede movement and reduce lifting capacity. It's often helpful to assess and address these factors in addition to CNS-based solutions.",
      "source": "target",
